 Task 3 — Quality by Environment
 Output:
 environment
 indoor     4.500000
 outdoor    3.250000
 Name: quality, dtype: float64
 * Which environment has the higher average quality? Indoor (average quality score of 4.5 vs. 3.25 for outdoor).
  * What does this tell you? Video recordings taken in indoor environments generally achieve higher quality scores than those taken outdoors.
  * What doesn't it tell you? It doesn't tell you why outdoor quality is lower—whether it is due to natural lighting/glare, or simply because lower-quality signs like HELP happened to be filmed outdoors.
Task 4 — Quality by Sign and Environment
 Output:
